{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"event","timestamp":"2026-10-24T10:39:15.988Z","data":{"event":{"id":"evt_16d7e4c11001urRT2QAMoYWfR0","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_e9281e02fffeDFzpb4jysElH7e","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1ab85f1e1f9e46ffa439956f7dcbe660","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"README.md","limit":240},"output":"<path>README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # CyberDAO Platform\n2: \n3: CyberDAO Platform is a full-stack governance application for CyberChain. It\n4: combines a CyberChain smart contract with a NestJS REST API, a Next.js DApp,\n5: PostgreSQL persistence, an external AI service, and a blockchain event indexer.\n6: \n7: The blockchain is the source of truth for governance authorization and voting.\n8: PostgreSQL is the indexed read model used for fast screens, reporting, transaction\n9: history, and synchronization state.\n10: \n11: ## Project purpose\n12: \n13: The project demonstrates a maintainable DAO workflow in which:\n14: \n15: - an administrator creates and publishes governance proposals;\n16: - eligible member wallets are assigned to individual proposals;\n17: - assigned members sign their own votes with MetaMask or CyberChain Wallet;\n18: - proposals, assignments, votes, and lifecycle actions are recorded on-chain;\n19: - confirmed transactions and events are indexed into PostgreSQL;\n20: - the DApp reads indexed data instead of repeatedly querying the blockchain.\n21: \n22: It uses clean architecture so domain and application rules do not depend on\n23: NestJS, PostgreSQL, Next.js, or the CyberChain SDK.\n24: \n25: ## Screenshots\n26: \n27: ### Governance dashboard\n28: \n29: The administrator dashboard summarizes proposals, active voting periods,\n30: eligible members, indexed votes, and manual blockchain synchronization.\n31: \n32: ![CyberDAO governance dashboard](docs/images/governance-dashboard.png)\n33: \n34: ### Proposal management\n35: \n36: The proposal workspace displays on-chain and draft proposals with their\n37: current governance status, voting options, and deadlines.\n38: \n39: ![CyberDAO proposal management](docs/images/proposals.png)\n40: \n41: ## Main use cases\n42: \n43: ### AI assistant\n44: \n45: The Next.js dashboard sends AI requests to the NestJS API. Nest validates the\n46: request, resolves the selected proposal to a trusted DAO scope, and forwards it\n47: to `api-ai-server`. The external service owns model providers, agents, tools,\n48: RAG, embeddings, citations, and blockchain-aware analysis. Nest does not run a\n49: local LLM or fall back to a native agent implementation.\n50: \n51: Linked proposal PDFs are uploaded to `api-ai-server` for indexing. Single-query\n52: responses are normalized for the frontend and recorded in the research-run\n53: history; batch responses are returned directly and are not persisted as single\n54: runs.\n55: \n56: ### Administrator\n57: \n58: - Connect the configured DAO administrator wallet.\n59: - Create a proposal with its title, purpose, description, type, voting period,\n60:   voting options, and initial eligible members.\n61: - Publish the proposal to CyberChain.\n62: - Assign or remove members before voting starts.\n63: - Vote when the administrator wallet is also an assigned member.\n64: - Cancel a proposal or finalize its result where the contract permits it.\n65: - Review proposal transactions and audit history.\n66: - Run an incremental blockchain synchronization into SQLite.\n67: \n68: ### Member\n69: \n70: - Connect a real wallet without sharing its private key with the API.\n71: - View assigned and active proposals.\n72: - Select an option and sign the vote transaction in the wallet.\n73: - Prevent duplicate votes through both application and contract validation.\n74: - View confirmed voting history, totals, and transaction hashes.\n75: \n76: ### Synchronization and indexing\n77: \n78: - Confirm wallet-submitted vote receipts.\n79: - Scan `VoteCast` events in RPC-safe block ranges.\n80: - Persist votes and chain transactions idempotently.\n81: - Resume incremental indexing from the last successful block.\n82: - Run automatically on an interval or manually from the admin dashboard/API.\n83: \n84: ## Technology\n85: \n86: - Node.js 20 or newer and npm workspaces\n87: - TypeScript\n88: - NestJS with Fastify for the API\n89: - Next.js App Router and React for the DApp\n90: - SQLite, Kysely, and `better-sqlite3`\n91: - Solidit","metadata":{"preview":"# CyberDAO Platform\n\nCyberDAO Platform is a full-stack governance application for CyberChain. It\ncombines a CyberChain smart contract with a NestJS REST API, a Next.js DApp,\nPostgreSQL persistence, an external AI service, and a blockchain event indexer.\n\nThe blockchain is the source of truth for governance authorization and voting.\nPostgreSQL is the indexed read model used for fast screens, reporting, transaction\nhistory, and synchronization state.\n\n## Project purpose\n\nThe project demonstrates a maintainable DAO workflow in which:\n\n- an administrator creates and publishes governance proposals;\n- eligible member wallets are assigned to individual proposals;\n- assigned members sign their own votes with MetaMask or CyberChain Wallet;\n- proposals, assignments, votes, and lifecycle actions are recorded on-chain;\n- confirmed transactions and events are indexed into PostgreSQL;\n- the DApp reads indexed data instead of repeatedly querying the blockchain.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"README.md","text":"# CyberDAO Platform\n\nCyberDAO Platform is a full-stack governance application for CyberChain. It\ncombines a CyberChain smart contract with a NestJS REST API, a Next.js DApp,\nPostgreSQL persistence, an external AI service, and a blockchain event indexer.\n\nThe blockchain is the source of truth for governance authorization and voting.\nPostgreSQL is the indexed read model used for fast screens, reporting, transaction\nhistory, and synchronization state.\n\n## Project purpose\n\nThe project demonstrates a maintainable DAO workflow in which:\n\n- an administrator creates and publishes governance proposals;\n- eligible member wallets are assigned to individual proposals;\n- assigned members sign their own votes with MetaMask or CyberChain Wallet;\n- proposals, assignments, votes, and lifecycle actions are recorded on-chain;\n- confirmed transactions and events are indexed into PostgreSQL;\n- the DApp reads indexed data instead of repeatedly querying the blockchain.\n\nIt uses clean architecture so domain and application rules do not depend on\nNestJS, PostgreSQL, Next.js, or the CyberChain SDK.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n### Governance dashboard\n\nThe administrator dashboard summarizes proposals, active voting periods,\neligible members, indexed votes, and manual blockchain synchronization.\n\n![CyberDAO governance dashboard](docs/images/governance-dashboard.png)\n\n### Proposal management\n\nThe proposal workspace displays on-chain and draft proposals with their\ncurrent governance status, voting options, and deadlines.\n\n![CyberDAO proposal management](docs/images/proposals.png)\n\n## Main use cases\n\n### AI assistant\n\nThe Next.js dashboard sends AI requests to the NestJS API. Nest validates the\nrequest, resolves the selected proposal to a trusted DAO scope, and forwards it\nto `api-ai-server`. The external service owns model providers, agents, tools,\nRAG, embeddings, citations, and blockchain-aware analysis. Nest does not run a\nlocal LLM or fall back to a native agent implementation.\n\nLinked proposal PDFs are uploaded to `api-ai-server` for indexing. Single-query\nresponses are normalized for the frontend and recorded in the research-run\nhistory; batch responses are returned directly and are not persisted as single\nruns.\n\n### Administrator\n\n- Connect the configured DAO administrator wallet.\n- Create a proposal with its title, purpose, description, type, voting period,\n  voting options, and initial eligible members.\n- Publish the proposal to CyberChain.\n- Assign or remove members before voting starts.\n- Vote when the administrator wallet is also an assigned member.\n- Cancel a proposal or finalize its result where the contract permits it.\n- Review proposal transactions and audit history.\n- Run an incremental blockchain synchronization into SQLite.\n\n### Member\n\n- Connect a real wallet without sharing its private key with the API.\n- View assigned and active proposals.\n- Select an option and sign the vote transaction in the wallet.\n- Prevent duplicate votes through both application and contract validation.\n- View confirmed voting history, totals, and transaction hashes.\n\n### Synchronization and indexing\n\n- Confirm wallet-submitted vote receipts.\n- Scan `VoteCast` events in RPC-safe block ranges.\n- Persist votes and chain transactions idempotently.\n- Resume incremental indexing from the last successful block.\n- Run automatically on an interval or manually from the admin dashboard/API.\n\n## Technology\n\n- Node.js 20 or newer and npm workspaces\n- TypeScript\n- NestJS with Fastify for the API\n- Next.js App Router and React for the DApp\n- SQLite, Kysely, and `better-sqlite3`\n- Solidity and OpenZeppelin\n- `@cyberchain/smart-contract-wrapper`\n- CyberChain Wallet and MetaMask adapters\n\n## Repository structure\n\n```text\ndao-platform/\n|-- apps/\n|   |-- api/                         NestJS REST API and background indexer\n|   `-- web/                         Next.js governance DApp\n|-- packages/\n|   |-- domain/                      Entities, value objects, and business rules\n|   |-- applicat","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":240,"totalLines":414,"truncated":true}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1792838355687,"end":1792838355984}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_034cc84c3e3e19f0016adc8ad4d7f88191a59901a32a491da8"}},"id":"prt_16d7e4ae0001QdNpLiFkfdvyjx","sessionID":"ses_e9281e02fffeDFzpb4jysElH7e","messageID":"msg_16d7e3b2a001FjU1Dhc0KK0Y7O"},"time":1792838355985}}}}
