{"record_type":"timeline-node","type":"tool-after","timestamp":"2026-10-24T10:40:25.576Z","data":{"input":{"tool":"read","sessionID":"ses_e9281e02fffeDFzpb4jysElH7e","callID":"call_56d0f4ba50f64972918f9a74b5a6c790","args":{"filePath":"README.md","offset":238,"limit":50}},"output":{"title":"README.md","output":"<path>README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n238: ## Database setup\n239: \n240: Run the migrations from the repository root:\n241: \n242: ```powershell\n243: npm run db:migrate --workspace=@dao-platform/database\n244: ```\n245: \n246: The migrations are applied to the database configured by `POSTGRES_URL`.\n247: \n248: ## Run the project\n249: \n250: Use two VS Code terminals from the repository root.\n251: \n252: Terminal 1 — start the API and background indexer:\n253: \n254: ```powershell\n255: npm run dev:api\n256: ```\n257: \n258: Terminal 2 — start the Next.js DApp:\n259: \n260: ```powershell\n261: npm run dev:web\n262: ```\n263: \n264: Open:\n265: \n266: ```text\n267: Frontend: http://localhost:3001\n268: API:      http://localhost:3000/v1\n269: Health:   http://localhost:3000/v1/health\n270: ```\n271: \n272: The browser first displays the wallet connection screen. The governance\n273: dashboard is shown only after a wallet is connected. The selected wallet type\n274: is remembered and restored after refresh while the extension remains unlocked.\n275: \n276: ## Governance workflow\n277: \n278: 1. Connect the configured administrator wallet.\n279: 2. Open **Proposals**.\n280: 3. Enter proposal details, two to ten voting options, a future voting period,\n281:    and initial member addresses.\n282: 4. Select **Create, publish & assign members**.\n283: 5. The API saves a draft, publishes the proposal, waits for confirmation, and\n284:    assigns the members on-chain.\n285: 6. Disconnect the administrator and connect an assigned member wallet.\n286: 7. Open the active proposal, choose an option, and approve the wallet signing\n287:    request.\n\n(Showing lines 238-287 of 414. Use offset=288 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Database setup\n\nRun the migrations from the repository root:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run db:migrate --workspace=@dao-platform/database\n```\n\nThe migrations are applied to the database configured by `POSTGRES_URL`.\n\n## Run the project\n\nUse two VS Code terminals from the repository root.\n\nTerminal 1 — start the API and background indexer:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run dev:api\n```\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"README.md","text":"## Database setup\n\nRun the migrations from the repository root:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run db:migrate --workspace=@dao-platform/database\n```\n\nThe migrations are applied to the database configured by `POSTGRES_URL`.\n\n## Run the project\n\nUse two VS Code terminals from the repository root.\n\nTerminal 1 — start the API and background indexer:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run dev:api\n```\n\nTerminal 2 — start the Next.js DApp:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run dev:web\n```\n\nOpen:\n\n```text\nFrontend: http://localhost:3001\nAPI:      http://localhost:3000/v1\nHealth:   http://localhost:3000/v1/health\n```\n\nThe browser first displays the wallet connection screen. The governance\ndashboard is shown only after a wallet is connected. The selected wallet type\nis remembered and restored after refresh while the extension remains unlocked.\n\n## Governance workflow\n\n1. Connect the configured administrator wallet.\n2. Open **Proposals**.\n3. Enter proposal details, two to ten voting options, a future voting period,\n   and initial member addresses.\n4. Select **Create, publish & assign members**.\n5. The API saves a draft, publishes the proposal, waits for confirmation, and\n   assigns the members on-chain.\n6. Disconnect the administrator and connect an assigned member wallet.\n7. Open the active proposal, choose an option, and approve the wallet signing\n   request.","lineStart":238,"lineEnd":287,"totalLines":414,"truncated":true}}}}}
